k(M*10^-6)":88.8,"IC50_Dark_value":88.8,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1039/d3qi02032k","Year":2024,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-048664","value":"4.2","numeric":4.2}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-985062","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"Cp-OAc","Cell_line":"NCI-H226","Time(h)":160,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"6.2 ± 1.1","IC50_Dark_value":6.2,"Method":"SRB","Notes":"Oxygen condition: normoxia; Culture model: Monolayer; Recovery after drug removal (h): 144; Drug removed before recovery/readout; Drug exposure before removal: 16 h","DOI":"10.1016/j.bcp.2005.07.016","Year":2005,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-985062","value":"1.3 ± 0.1","numeric":1.3}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-985063","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"Cp-OAc","Cell_line":"NCI-H226","Time(h)":160,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"8.4 ± 3.6","IC50_Dark_value":8.4,"Method":"SRB","Notes":"O2: 0.1%; Oxygen condition: hypoxia; Culture model: Monolayer; Recovery after drug removal (h): 144; Drug removed before recovery/readout; Drug exposure before removal: 16 h","DOI":"10.1016/j.bcp.2005.07.016","Year":2005,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-985063","value":"1.5 ± 0.3","numeric":1.5}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-985078","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"Cp-OAc","Cell_line":"NCI-H520","Time(h)":160,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"4.4 ± 1.1","IC50_Dark_value":4.4,"Method":"SRB","Notes":"Oxygen condition: normoxia; Culture model: Monolayer; Recovery after drug removal (h): 144; Drug removed before recovery/readout; Drug exposure before removal: 16 h","DOI":"10.1016/j.bcp.2005.07.016","Year":2005,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-985078","value":"0.9 ± 0.1","numeric":0.9}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-985079","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"Cp-OAc","Cell_line":"NCI-H520","Time(h)":160,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"4.9 ± 0.9","IC50_Dark_value":4.9,"Method":"SRB","Notes":"O2: 0.1%; Oxygen condition: hypoxia; Culture model: Monolayer; Recovery after drug removal (h): 144; Drug removed before recovery/readout; Drug exposure before removal: 16 h","DOI":"10.1016/j.bcp.2005.07.016","Year":2005,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-985079","value":"1.3 ± 0.2","numeric":1.3}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":5,"value":-2,"value_relation":"=","std":0.18,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"0.9% NaCl","doi":"10.1021/jm300580y","year":2012,"record_id":"MLDB-001844","detection":"ICP-OES","method_description":"The Log Pow determination of platinum(IV) compounds were conducted using the shake flask method. (57) Platinum(IV) compounds were dissolved in 0.9% NaCl w/v ultrapure water (presaturated with n-octanol for 96 h and left to stand overnight). The solutions were sonicated and filtered through Celite to remove undissolved platinum(IV) compounds. The initial concentrations of platinum content were determined by ICP-OES. Subsequently, the platinum(IV) solutions were added an equal volume of n-octanol (presaturated with 0.9% NaCl w/v ultrapure water for 96 h and left to stand overnight). The heterogeneous mixtures were shaken vigorously for 2 h before centrifuging at 4200g for 15 min to achieve phase separation. The final concentration of platinum content in the aqueous phase was determined again by ICP-OES, and the water–octanol partition coefficient was calculated. All experiments were done in triplicates."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"cis,trans,cis-[PtCl2(OAc)2(NH3)2]","value":-2.2,"value_relation":"=","std":0.024,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"150 mM KCl","doi":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2004.05.017","year":2004,"record_id":"MLDB-001927","detection":"GFAAS","method_description":"The lipophilicity parameter, log Poct, of the eight complexes was determined by measuring in triplicate the partition coefficients of the 1-octanol/water system based on the method reported by Robillard et al. [27]. The solutions were made up to 500 ml (100 μM) in 0.15 M KCl (7.5 × 10-2 mol, 5.59 g) in order to minimise aquation of the complexes. Equal volumes (2 ml) of the aqueous solution and 1-octanol were shaken together mechanically for 24 h. Aliquots were taken from the upper octanol layer and the lower aqueous layer. The water samples were diluted 100-fold with rigorous shaking. Platinum content was determined by graphite furnace atomic absorption spectroscopy (GFAAS). The partition coefficients were expressed as the log10 of the ratio of the platinum concentration in the 1-octanol layer to the platinum concentration in the aqueous layer according to Eq. (1)."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"cisPt(Ac)2","value":-1.85,"value_relation":"=","std":0.09,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"200 mM NaCl","temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1016/j.bcp.2015.04.003","year":2015,"record_id":"MLDB-002156","detection":"FAAS","method_description":"To determine the partition coefficient (P) the shake flask method was used. Octanol-saturated water (OSW) and water-saturated octanol (WSO) were prepared using analytical grade octanol and 0.2 M aqueous NaCl solution (to suppress hydrolysis of the chlorido complexes). Compounds were first dissolved in DMF (compounds cisPt(Ac)(VPA) and cisPt(VPA)2) or water (cisPt(Ac)2 and cisplatin). Mixing was done by vortexing for 30 min at room temperature to establish the partition equilibrium. To separate the phases, centrifugation was done at 3000 × g for 5 min. The aqueous layer was carefully separated from the octanol layer for platinum analysis. Pt was quantified from aliquots taken from the octanol-saturated aqueous samples before and after partition by FAAS. Partition coefficients of Pt complexes were calculated using the equation log P = log ([Pt]WSO/[Pt]OSW)."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":1,"value":-1.921,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","pH":7,"doi":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2014.07.018","year":2014,"record_id":"MLDB-002201","detection":"ICP-OES","method_description":"The partition coefficient of compounds 1–3 was measured by the shake-flask method. A mixture of equal volumes of n-octanol and water was shaken at room temperature for 24 h on a mechanical shaker in order to saturate each phase with the other phase. The mixture was centrifugated for the separation of phases. For each compound, a stock solution in water pre-saturated with n-octanol was prepared. A volume (Vwater) of this solution was shaken for 30 min with a volume of water-saturated n-octanol (Voct). Usually, the volumes of n-octanol and water are equal, but for compounds with extreme log Po/w values different volumes must be used (in the actual case, Vwater/Voct = 1/19 for 1, 1/1 for 2 and 9/1 for 3). Phase separation was carried out by the centrifugation of the vessels for 30 min at 4000 rpm. The platinum content in the initial ([C]init.water) and final ([C]fin.water) aqueous phases was determined by means of inductively coupled plasma-optical emission spectrometry (ICP-OES). The log Po/w values were calculated with the following formula:"}]}